            "title": "Linear System",
            "description": "Solve `x' = 2x + y`, `y' = x + 2y` using diagonalization.",
            "difficulty": "medium",
            "points": 14,
            "solutionSteps": [
                "Step 1: Matrix `A=\\begin{pmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\end{pmatrix}` has eigenvalues `3,1`",
                "Step 2: Eigenvectors provide decoupled system",
                "Step 3: General solution combination of `e^{3t}` and `e^{t}`"
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 5,
            "topic": "Laplace Transform",
            "title": "Solving with Laplace",
            "description": "Solve `y' + 2y = u(t)` with `y(0)=0` using Laplace transform (`u` is the unit step function).",
            "difficulty": "medium",
            "points": 12,
            "solutionSteps": [
                "Step 1: Laplace: `sY - y(0) + 2Y = \\frac{1}{s}`",
                "Step 2: `Y = \\frac{1}{s(s+2)}`",
                "Step 3: Inverse transform: `y(t) = \\tfrac{1}{2}(1 - e^{-2t})`"
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 6,
            "topic": "PDE",
            "title": "Heat equation (outline)",
            "description": "Give the separated solutions for `u_t = k u_{xx}` on `0<x<L` with homogeneous Dirichlet boundary conditions.",
            "difficulty": "medium",
            "points": 12,
            "solutionSteps": [
                "Step 1: Ansatz `u(x,t)=X(x)T(t)`",
                "Step 2: `X'' + \\lambda X=0` with `X(0)=X(L)=0` gives `X_n=\\sin(\\tfrac{n\\pi x}{L})`",
                "Step 3: `T_n(t)=e^{-k (n\\pi/L)^2 t}`, general series solution"
            ]
        }
    ]
